# GCC pass dumps are named after the source (for example,
# 08120454.c.12.life) and are emitted into the compiler's working directory.
# Ignore them repository-wide so a diagnostic compile from any directory cannot
# flood Git status. The digit after `.c.` keeps ordinary numbered C sources live.
*.c.[0-9]*.*
tools/scratch/*
!tools/scratch/README.md

# Rust tooling
target/
*.rlib
*.rmeta
*.pdb

# Worktree convenience symlink to the shared ROM set.
/roms

# Adoption's per-overlay lock (see tools/alchemy/src/overlay). Lives
# beside the tracked assembly it guards, so it must never become committable.
games/*/assets/code/*.adopt-lock
/games/tbs/SRC/GRAPHICS/COMMON/STILL.PNG
/games/tbs/SRC/GRAPHICS/COMMON/TILE.PNG
/games/tbs/SRC/GRAPHICS/COMMON/PORTRAIT.PNG
